<section class="ls-sheet" aria-labelledby="h-log">
<header class="ls-sh">
<span class="ls-sh-n" aria-hidden="true">07</span>
<h2 class="ls-sh-t" id="h-log">The race, hour by hour</h2>
<span class="ls-sh-m" data-tpl="led.secLogNote">67 hours</span>
</header>
<div data-block="log">
<div class="ls-lg">
<div class="ls-lg-y">
<span class="ls-seg">01</span>
<span class="ls-lg-c">Fri 12:00</span>
</div>
<div>
<h3 class="ls-lg-t">93 souls start</h3>
<p class="ls-lg-b">Friday 3 October 2025, 12:00. The debut edition sets off on a 6.7 km loop in Bornheim.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="ls-lg">
<div class="ls-lg-y">
<span class="ls-seg">18</span>
<span class="ls-lg-c">Sat 05:00</span>
</div>
<div>
<h3 class="ls-lg-t">Women&#39;s podium settled</h3>
<p class="ls-lg-b">Mia Walsoe Lehn and Paulina Zäck both finish 18 laps, 120.7 km.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="ls-lg">
<div class="ls-lg-y">
<span class="ls-seg">20</span>
<span class="ls-lg-c">Sat 07:00</span>
</div>
<div>
<h3 class="ls-lg-t">Last woman standing</h3>
<p class="ls-lg-b">Kathrin Reichelt stops at 20 laps and 134.1 km, first among the women.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="ls-lg">
<div class="ls-lg-y">
<span class="ls-seg">28</span>
<span class="ls-lg-c">Sat 15:00</span>
</div>
<div>
<h3 class="ls-lg-t">Ten past 28</h3>
<p class="ls-lg-b">Ten runners pass 28 laps — more than 187 km of continuous hourly running.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="ls-lg">
<div class="ls-lg-y">
<span class="ls-seg">40</span>
<span class="ls-lg-c">Sun 03:00</span>
</div>
<div>
<h3 class="ls-lg-t">Third place decided</h3>
<p class="ls-lg-b">Pierre Biege is out at 40 laps, leaving Gottwald and Elosrouti alone in the race.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="ls-lg">
<div class="ls-lg-y">
<span class="ls-seg">67</span>
<span class="ls-lg-c">Mon 06:00</span>
</div>
<div>
<h3 class="ls-lg-t">One soul left</h3>
<p class="ls-lg-b">Gottwald finishes lap 67 in 66:52 and is ready to start lap 68. Elosrouti withdraws with an inflamed Achilles and the first Last Soul Ultra has its winner.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
